        "Third, Boundary Jumping via Home and End: Pressing Home instantly jumps the highlight to the very first option (index 0); pressing End instantly jumps to the very last option. However, care must be taken: if the user is actively typing in the text input and has text in the buffer, Home and End should manipulate the text cursor position within the string unless combined with a modifier key like Alt+Home or Ctrl+Home, preventing interference with standard text editing.",
        "Fourth, Selection Toggling via Space and Enter: When an option has virtual focus, pressing Enter commits the highlighted option into the selected token list. In multi-select modes, pressing Space toggles the checkbox selection state without closing the popup menu, allowing the user to select multiple items in rapid succession without reopening the dropdown repeatedly.",
